<%# ** THE GIVE-WAY ORDER: every category a rule claims for, in the order they give way (§4).
    Local: `groups` (BudgetPagePresenter::Group list).

    IT WAS THE FILL ORDER AND THE LIST IS THE SAME LIST. A distribution used to walk it handing
    money out, lowest priority first; nothing is handed out any more (computed-claims spec §5).
    What priority still decides is what §4 keeps it for: when a user's claims outrun their money,
    `HomePresenter#uncovered_claims` walks this order BACKWARDS and names the categories nothing
    covers — so the card at the BOTTOM is the one that gives way first. `Category.in_fill_order`
    ranks every holder against every other over ONE list, and what is inside this element is
    exactly what `PATCH /budget/reorder` rewrites.

    The form is EMPTY and hidden: reorder_controller fills it with one `category_ids[]` per card in
    DOM order at drop time. The ▲▼ buttons carry their own already-swapped list (see
    BudgetPageHelper#reordered_category_ids) so the order is reachable with no JavaScript at all —
    the drag is the enhancement, not the mechanism. %>
<section class="space-y-3" data-fill-order
         data-controller="app--budget-page--reorder"
         data-action="dragover->app--budget-page--reorder#over
                      drop->app--budget-page--reorder#drop">
  <%# STACKS BELOW `sm` (design review H5). The eyebrow and its eighteen-word instruction were on
      one baseline row: at 375px the instruction squeezed into a two-word column beside "FILL
      ORDER" and ran to five lines. `text-gray-500` rather than `-400`, which measured 2.9:1 on
      white — a hint nobody could read is not a quieter hint. %>
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:justify-between gap-1 sm:gap-4 px-1">
    <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-500">Give-way order</h2>
    <p class="text-xs text-gray-500">Drag a card, or use the arrows, to set which gives way first when you run short</p>
  </div>

  <% groups.each do |group| %>
    <%= render "category_group", group: group, groups: groups %>
  <% end %>

  <% form_data = { app__budget_page__reorder_target: "form" } %>
  <%= form_with(url: budget_page_reorder_path, method: :patch, class: "hidden", data: form_data) do %>
    <%# One hidden `category_ids[]` per card, appended by reorder_controller in DOM order at drop. %>
  <% end %>
</section>
